This product includes software and data derived from EcoLogits
(https://ecologits.ai, https://github.com/genai-impact/ecologits), developed by
GenAI Impact and licensed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0).

Specifically:

  * The environmental-impact methodology and its numeric coefficients used in
    eco_impact_filter.py (the GPU/server energy and embodied-impact model) are
    vendored from EcoLogits, file ecologits/impacts/llm.py, at commit
    42154236c3b275346e8b97b04f49cd19877316e6.

  * scripts/sync-eco-models.py downloads, and the generated registry
    (examples/eco_models.json) redistributes, EcoLogits' model-parameter data
    (models.json) and electricity-mix data (electricity_mixes.json) from the
    same source.

The EcoLogits methodology is described in their documentation and publications;
please cite EcoLogits if you use these estimates in research. If EcoLogits'
coefficients, data, or method change upstream, re-run scripts/sync-eco-models.py
and refresh the vendored coefficients in eco_impact_filter.py accordingly.

Because this derived material is MPL-2.0, this project is released under
MPL-2.0 as well (see LICENSE).

Original contributions by CUNY AI Lab (also MPL-2.0):
  * the Open WebUI Filter integration and status-line presentation,
  * the model-id matching + registry-loading + graceful-fallback logic,
  * scripts/sync-eco-models.py (the sync/coverage tooling) and
    scripts/eco-extra-patterns.json (curated parameter estimates for models
